Six JSON files come from internal/playback/testdata/protocol_v3. Three are
also published byte-identically under docs/design/schemas/playback-v3/v3/fixtures/valid;
attempt_keys.json, conformance_matrix.json and subtitle_inventory.json exist only
under testdata, so the testdata directory is the single copy source.

decision_response.json and native-decision_response.json are not vendored:
they are the protocol domain's decision with API-relative media URLs and
integer file ids, which is what the retired v1 routes returned. The client
now decodes the v2 decision; its fixture is
Tests/Fixtures/APIv2/playback_start_opaque_ids.json.

capability_response.json is not vendored: it is the retired v1 capability
document. The v2 capability fixtures live in Tests/Fixtures/APIv2.

error_response.json is not vendored: it is the retired v1 426
client_upgrade_required envelope. v2 errors are problem documents.

Refresh these files together from the server, then regenerate Silo.xcodeproj with cd iosApp && xcodegen generate.

